# L §4.4 (tally 2.1.8 R13, X1, X2; K1, the gate's m2_gate_w1 w10): a window shifted by a computation carries the
# name it was computed from. add_business(wd, 1, cal) prints window(2026-03-30, 2026-04-06), nobody's name; it
# carries wd, and windows each takes wd. The same lines as 2.1.7's refcore.
=== m.tally
model w_each
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source card "invented"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

axis ax
  lo "low"
  hi "high"

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place work: outside lives 1900-01-01..

input cal: calendar
input pd: date
input wd: date
input rate: money PLN
input twice: int

def bonus_amt: money PLN at wd
  rule base = rate
  rule hi beats base = rate * twice when ax == hi

move bonus: transfers
  on pd
  at wd
  leg cash from work to konto amount rate

move gift: transfers
  on wd
  leg cash from work to konto amount bonus_amt


version v
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  cal = calendar(weekends [sat, sun], added [window(2026-06-01, 2026-06-02)]) "c"
  pd = 2026-04-01 "c"
  wd = window(2026-03-28, 2026-04-03) "c"
  twice = 2 "c"
  opening[konto] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "own"

version r1
  cite card
  governs ..2026-03-31
  known 2026-01-01
  rate = 10.00 PLN "c"

version r2
  cite card
  governs 2026-04-01..
  known 2026-01-01
  rate = 12.00 PLN "c"
ask w10p: add_business(wd, 1, cal)
ask w10: add_business(wd, 1, cal) windows each
=== expect
w10 [wd = 2026-03-28 .. 2026-03-29]: 2026-03-30
  cut 2026-03-01
w10 [wd = 2026-03-30]: 2026-03-31
  cut 2026-03-01
w10 [wd = 2026-03-31]: 2026-04-01
  cut 2026-03-01
w10 [wd = 2026-04-01]: 2026-04-02
  cut 2026-03-01
w10 [wd = 2026-04-02]: 2026-04-03
  cut 2026-03-01
w10 [wd = 2026-04-03]: 2026-04-06
  cut 2026-03-01
w10p: window(2026-03-30, 2026-04-06)
  cut 2026-03-01
